-- title:
--   Definitions for Exact synthesis of single-qubit unitaries over Clifford-cyclotomic gate sets
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Exact synthesis of single-qubit unitaries over Clifford-cyclotomic gate sets* (arXiv:1501.04944) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `BlochMat`
--   - `hZero`: The paper's H0, including its absolute phase, equation (2), PDF p.4.
--   - `cliffordGroup`: Exactly <H0,S>, using each generator and its adjoint, PDF p.4. The monoid closure is the group generated by these unitary matrices.
--   - `cyclotomicZRotation`: Uz(theta)=diag(1,exp(i theta)), equation (4), PDF p.4.
--   - `cyclotomicRoot`: The root zeta_m=exp(2 pi i/m), PDF p.4; only positive m occurs in results.
--   - `cyclotomicSynthesisRing`: R_n as an actual subring of C, PDF p.4.
--   - `integerRing`: Z[zeta_(2n)], PDF pp.19,21.
--   - `cyclotomicGroup`: G_n=<C,Uz(pi/n)>, equation (3), PDF p.4. Adjoint generators implement inverses.
--   - `ringUnitaries`: Actual U_2(R_n), with no quotient by scalar phase, PDF pp.3,12.
--   - `positiveAxisRotation`: Positive-axis rotations, equation before (6), PDF p.5.
--   - `homomorphicBloch`: Homomorphic Bloch representation. Printed (9) has transposed indices; changed to Re tr(P_i U P_j U†)/2 because pp.11,17 use left cancellation and row patterns. This source correction requires independent moderation.
--   - `blochCliffords`: Image of the specifically generated Clifford group, PDF p.6.
--   - `PhaseEquivalent`: Equality up to a single global phase, PDF p.5.
--   - `SynthesisLetter`: Gate words for Definition 2.1, PDF p.5. A rotation letter has positive unit cost; any member of the source's precise Clifford group has cost zero.
--   - `synthesisWordMatrix`: A word is multiplied in the source's printed left-to-right order, PDF p.5.
--   - `synthesisWordCost`: Actual number of elementary Uz(pi/n) occurrences, PDF p.5.
--   - `minimumRotationCost`: T_n(U), the least achievable word cost modulo global phase, PDF p.5. The fallback 0 is off-domain only: all uses below assume U in G_n, where a positive-letter word exists (inverse rotations have finite order 2n).
--   - `canonicalProduct`: Product of canonical rotations in printed order, equation (14), PDF p.7.
--   - `IsCyclotomicCanonical`: Precisely the canonical-form constraints; optimality is not a premise, Lemma 3.1, PDF p.7. The empty list is allowed.
--   - `canonicalCost`: The canonical non-Clifford cost, equation (24), PDF p.10.
--   - `IsTwoPower`: Power-of-two test, equations (23),(32), PDF pp.10,15.
--   - `denominatorWeight`: q_a, equation (23), PDF p.10, verified in the PDF. The quotient is n/gcd(a,n). For valid a and n=2^k s, a power-of-two quotient has 2<=j<=k, so both natural subtractions here agree with integer subtraction.
--   - `denominatorBeta`: beta, equation (23), PDF p.10; k is positive in every use.
--   - `denominatorAlpha`: alpha=2^(2^(1-k))=2^(1/2^(k-1)), PDF p.15; no natural negative power.
--   - `cosineNumerator`: c_a, equivalently equation (33), PDF p.15. This is exactly the piecewise normalization (32), with exponent 1-2^(1-j) in its power-of-two branch.
--   - `sineNumerator`: s_a with the same normalization, equations (32),(33), PDF p.15.
--   - `realCyclotomicField`: Frac(R_n intersect R), realized inside C, PDF pp.10,18. The smallest subfield containing the real subring is its fraction field.
--   - `numeratorField`: The larger field K=Q({c_a,s_a},alpha), PDF p.15.
--   - `InIntegers`: Algebraic integrality in the named field, Appendix A, PDF pp.28-29.
--   - `IntegerDivides`: Divisibility requires nonzero divisor and integral quotient in F, Definition A.2, PDF pp.9,28. This is not divisibility in C.
--   - `IntegerCoprime`: Principal-ideal coprimality, expressed by the equivalent Bezout identity in O_F, Definition A.5, PDF p.29.
--   - `IntegerUnit`: Unit in O_F, rather than a nonzero element of C, PDF p.15.
--   - `ReducedDenominator`: A nonzero entry and a beta/alpha-reduced numerator, PDF pp.10,16.
--   - `RowHasExponent`: Row contains an entry with reduced exponent r, PDF p.10.
--   - `RowHasCoprime`: Row contains an entry whose normalized numerator is coprime to the base, PDF pp.10,17. Zero entries are explicitly excluded.
--   - `DenominatorPattern`: All three clauses of Theorems 4.1 and 6.3, PDF pp.10,16-17. Every comparison ranges over reduced nonzero entries. Row coprimality and attainment of both maxima are retained, not just a row upper bound.
--   - `canonicalTotalWeight`: N=sum q_ai, PDF p.10.
--   - `MinusOneIsTwoPower`: Positive t with 2^t=-1 modulo the odd part s; add 1 avoids natural negative integers. For s=1 this is true, as required, PDF p.13.
--   - `zRotationsIn`: Actual z-rotations inside a matrix group, PDF p.12.
--   - `finiteZRotations`: Equation (27), with endpoint represented by Fin(2n), PDF p.12.
--   - `finitePhases`: Equation (30), actual roots of unity, PDF p.13.
--   - `unitPhases`: Elements of R_n of complex modulus one, PDF p.13.
--   - `equalityFraction`: f_N, PDF pp.13-14. N is cast before division. All uses have N positive even.
--   - `SmallParameter`: Exactly the five parameters of Section 7 Parts 2-3, PDF pp.19-23.
--   - `twoPrime`: The unique prime above 2 on the five parameters, PDF p.19. Intersection of all primes containing 2 specifies it without choosing a prime or assuming the source's uniqueness result as an input. Outside those parameters no theorem uses this helper.
--   - `integralValuation`: Exponent of the prime ideal in an integral principal ideal, Definition 7.2, PDF p.19. emultiplicity uses ideal multiplication, not element divisibility.
--   - `extendedOrder`: Extended embedding that preserves infinity, PDF p.19.
--   - `primeValuation`: Additive ideal-normalized valuation on R_n, Definition 7.2, PDF p.19. A least dyadic denominator clears z, then its contribution to the valuation is subtracted. Both integral valuations are finite for nonzero arguments on the five parameters. Zero stays +infinity. The off-ring value is -infinity and is never used by the source statements.
--   - `columnComplexity`: mu(x,y)=-min(v_p(x),v_p(y)), Definition 7.3, PDF p.20. Normalized pairs have finite complexity even when one coordinate is zero.
--   - `smallComplexity`: mu_n=v_p(1+i), PDF p.20.
--   - `IsBinaryRepresentative`: Literal binary integral-basis representative of Z[zeta_(2n)] mod 2, PDF pp.21-22. It is an actual complex number, not an abstract residue class.
--   - `NormSumEven`: Mod 2 of the whole squared-modulus sum is zero, Lemma 7.5, PDF p.22.
--   - `reducedColumn`: The constructed pair (c_k,d_k), with order H0*Uz essential, PDF p.22.
-- source:
--   Exact synthesis of single-qubit unitaries over Clifford-cyclotomic gate sets, arXiv:1501.04944v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.04944v2

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_Gates
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_QubitBlochMaps

/-!
Statement targets from Forest--Gosset--Kliuchnikov--McKinnon,
arXiv:1501.04944v2. Two encoding-level algorithm targets are explicitly deferred.
The frozen ordered Pauli basis is imported from QAlgorithms.Defs.QubitBlochMaps.
Paper-specific names distinguish concepts from unrelated frozen short names.
The Bloch map uses the homomorphic trace convention required by the source proof;
this transposes printed equation (9) and the printed elementary rotations.
Compilation and independent moderation are pending the batch handoff.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intakenext100.P03

open scoped BigOperators Classical

-- Reuse the Mathlib matrix type without declaring a second Mat.
local notation "Mat" => Matrix Bool Bool ℂ

abbrev BlochMat := Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ

/-- The paper's H0, including its absolute phase, equation (2), PDF p.4. -/
def hZero : Mat :=
  fun a b => if a && b then -(1 + Complex.I) / 2 else (1 + Complex.I) / 2

/-- Exactly <H0,S>, using each generator and its adjoint, PDF p.4.
The monoid closure is the group generated by these unitary matrices. -/
def cliffordGroup : Submonoid Mat :=
  Submonoid.closure ({hZero, QAlgorithms.phaseS, star hZero,
    star QAlgorithms.phaseS} : Set Mat)

/-- Uz(theta)=diag(1,exp(i theta)), equation (4), PDF p.4. -/
def cyclotomicZRotation (theta : ℝ) : Mat :=
  Matrix.diagonal fun b => if b then Complex.exp (Complex.I * (theta : ℂ)) else 1

/-- The root zeta_m=exp(2 pi i/m), PDF p.4; only positive m occurs in results. -/
def cyclotomicRoot (m : ℕ) : ℂ := Complex.exp (2 * Real.pi * Complex.I / (m : ℂ))

/-- R_n as an actual subring of C, PDF p.4. -/
def cyclotomicSynthesisRing (n : ℕ) : Subring ℂ :=
  Subring.closure ({cyclotomicRoot (2 * n), (2 : ℂ)⁻¹} : Set ℂ)

/-- Z[zeta_(2n)], PDF pp.19,21. -/
def integerRing (n : ℕ) : Subring ℂ :=
  Subring.closure ({cyclotomicRoot (2 * n)} : Set ℂ)

/-- G_n=<C,Uz(pi/n)>, equation (3), PDF p.4. Adjoint generators implement inverses. -/
def cyclotomicGroup (n : ℕ) : Submonoid Mat :=
  Submonoid.closure ((cliffordGroup : Set Mat) ∪
    {cyclotomicZRotation (Real.pi / n), star (cyclotomicZRotation (Real.pi / n))})

/-- Actual U_2(R_n), with no quotient by scalar phase, PDF pp.3,12. -/
def ringUnitaries (n : ℕ) : Set Mat :=
  {U | U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup Bool ℂ ∧ ∀ i j, U i j ∈ cyclotomicSynthesisRing n}

-- Ordered X,Y,Z coordinates (PDF p.4) reuse frozen QubitChannels.sigma.

/-- Positive-axis rotations, equation before (6), PDF p.5. -/
def positiveAxisRotation (p : Fin 3) (theta : ℝ) : Mat :=
  ((1 + Complex.exp (Complex.I * (theta : ℂ))) / 2) • (1 : Mat) +
    ((1 - Complex.exp (Complex.I * (theta : ℂ))) / 2) • QAlgorithms.QubitChannels.sigma p

/-- Homomorphic Bloch representation. Printed (9) has transposed indices;
changed to Re tr(P_i U P_j U†)/2 because pp.11,17 use left cancellation and
row patterns. This source correction requires independent moderation. -/
def homomorphicBloch (U : Mat) : BlochMat :=
  fun i j => (Matrix.trace (QAlgorithms.QubitChannels.sigma i * U * QAlgorithms.QubitChannels.sigma j * star U)).re / 2

/-- Image of the specifically generated Clifford group, PDF p.6. -/
def blochCliffords : Set BlochMat := {M | ∃ C ∈ cliffordGroup, homomorphicBloch C = M}

/-- Equality up to a single global phase, PDF p.5. -/
def PhaseEquivalent (U V : Mat) : Prop :=
  ∃ phi : ℝ, U = Complex.exp (Complex.I * (phi : ℂ)) • V

/-- Gate words for Definition 2.1, PDF p.5. A rotation letter has positive unit
cost; any member of the source's precise Clifford group has cost zero. -/
inductive SynthesisLetter where
  | clifford : {C : Mat // C ∈ cliffordGroup} → SynthesisLetter
  | rotation : SynthesisLetter

/-- A word is multiplied in the source's printed left-to-right order, PDF p.5. -/
def synthesisWordMatrix (n : ℕ) (w : List SynthesisLetter) : Mat :=
  (w.map fun g => match g with
    | .clifford C => C.val
    | .rotation => cyclotomicZRotation (Real.pi / n)).prod

/-- Actual number of elementary Uz(pi/n) occurrences, PDF p.5. -/
def synthesisWordCost (w : List SynthesisLetter) : ℕ :=
  (w.map fun g => match g with
    | .clifford _ => 0
    | .rotation => 1).sum

/-- T_n(U), the least achievable word cost modulo global phase, PDF p.5.
The fallback 0 is off-domain only: all uses below assume U in G_n, where a
positive-letter word exists (inverse rotations have finite order 2n). -/
def minimumRotationCost (n : ℕ) (U : Mat) : ℕ :=
  if h : ∃ c : ℕ, ∃ w : List SynthesisLetter,
      synthesisWordCost w = c ∧ PhaseEquivalent U (synthesisWordMatrix n w)
  then Nat.find h else 0

/-- Canonical data: the axis/exponent list and the actual residual matrix D,
not a nonunique phase/Clifford witness pair, PDF pp.6-7. -/
local notation "CanonicalData" => List (Fin 3 × ℕ) × Matrix Bool Bool ℂ

/-- Product of canonical rotations in printed order, equation (14), PDF p.7. -/
def canonicalProduct (n : ℕ) (d : CanonicalData) : Mat :=
  (d.1.map fun pa => positiveAxisRotation pa.1 (pa.2 * Real.pi / n)).prod

/-- Precisely the canonical-form constraints; optimality is not a premise,
Lemma 3.1, PDF p.7. The empty list is allowed. -/
def IsCyclotomicCanonical (n : ℕ) (U : Mat) (d : CanonicalData) : Prop :=
  (∀ pa ∈ d.1, 1 ≤ pa.2 ∧ pa.2 < n / 2) ∧
  (∀ i : ℕ, ∀ x y : Fin 3 × ℕ,
    d.1[i]? = some x → d.1[i + 1]? = some y → x.1 ≠ y.1) ∧
  (∃ phi : ℝ, Complex.exp (Complex.I * (phi : ℂ)) • d.2 ∈ cliffordGroup) ∧
  U = canonicalProduct n d * d.2

/-- The canonical non-Clifford cost, equation (24), PDF p.10. -/
def canonicalCost (n : ℕ) (d : CanonicalData) : ℕ :=
  (d.1.map fun pa => min pa.2 (n / 2 - pa.2)).sum

/-- Power-of-two test, equations (23),(32), PDF pp.10,15. -/
def IsTwoPower (d : ℕ) : Prop := ∃ j : ℕ, d = 2 ^ j

/-- q_a, equation (23), PDF p.10, verified in the PDF. The quotient is
n/gcd(a,n). For valid a and n=2^k s, a power-of-two quotient has 2<=j<=k,
so both natural subtractions here agree with integer subtraction. -/
def denominatorWeight (n k a : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  if IsTwoPower (n / Nat.gcd a n) then
    2 ^ (k - 1) - 2 ^ (k - Nat.log 2 (n / Nat.gcd a n))
  else 2 ^ (k - 1)

/-- beta, equation (23), PDF p.10; k is positive in every use. -/
def denominatorBeta (k : ℕ) : ℂ :=
  if k = 1 then 2 else ((2 * Real.cos (Real.pi / (2 : ℝ) ^ k) : ℝ) : ℂ)

/-- alpha=2^(2^(1-k))=2^(1/2^(k-1)), PDF p.15; no natural negative power. -/
def denominatorAlpha (k : ℕ) : ℂ := ((2 : ℝ) ^ (1 / (2 : ℝ) ^ (k - 1)) : ℝ)

/-- c_a, equivalently equation (33), PDF p.15. This is exactly the piecewise
normalization (32), with exponent 1-2^(1-j) in its power-of-two branch. -/
def cosineNumerator (n k a : ℕ) : ℂ :=
  denominatorAlpha k ^ denominatorWeight n k a * (Real.cos (Real.pi * a / n) : ℂ)

/-- s_a with the same normalization, equations (32),(33), PDF p.15. -/
def sineNumerator (n k a : ℕ) : ℂ :=
  denominatorAlpha k ^ denominatorWeight n k a * (Real.sin (Real.pi * a / n) : ℂ)

/-- Frac(R_n intersect R), realized inside C, PDF pp.10,18. The smallest
subfield containing the real subring is its fraction field. -/
def realCyclotomicField (n : ℕ) : Subfield ℂ :=
  Subfield.closure {z | z ∈ cyclotomicSynthesisRing n ∧ z.im = 0}

/-- The larger field K=Q({c_a,s_a},alpha), PDF p.15. -/
def numeratorField (n k : ℕ) : Subfield ℂ :=
  Subfield.closure {z | z = denominatorAlpha k ∨ ∃ a : ℕ, 1 ≤ a ∧ a < n / 2 ∧
    (z = cosineNumerator n k a ∨ z = sineNumerator n k a)}

/-- Algebraic integrality in the named field, Appendix A, PDF pp.28-29. -/
def InIntegers (F : Subfield ℂ) (z : ℂ) : Prop := z ∈ F ∧ IsIntegral ℤ z

/-- Divisibility requires nonzero divisor and integral quotient in F,
Definition A.2, PDF pp.9,28. This is not divisibility in C. -/
def IntegerDivides (F : Subfield ℂ) (b w : ℂ) : Prop :=
  InIntegers F b ∧ InIntegers F w ∧ b ≠ 0 ∧
    ∃ q : ℂ, InIntegers F q ∧ w = b * q

/-- Principal-ideal coprimality, expressed by the equivalent Bezout identity
in O_F, Definition A.5, PDF p.29. -/
def IntegerCoprime (F : Subfield ℂ) (w b : ℂ) : Prop :=
  InIntegers F w ∧ InIntegers F b ∧ ∃ u v : ℂ,
    InIntegers F u ∧ InIntegers F v ∧ u * w + v * b = 1

/-- Unit in O_F, rather than a nonzero element of C, PDF p.15. -/
def IntegerUnit (F : Subfield ℂ) (w : ℂ) : Prop :=
  InIntegers F w ∧ ∃ v : ℂ, InIntegers F v ∧ w * v = 1

/-- A nonzero entry and a beta/alpha-reduced numerator, PDF pp.10,16. -/
def ReducedDenominator (F : Subfield ℂ) (b : ℂ) (z : ℝ) (r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  z ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ w : ℂ, InIntegers F w ∧ ¬ IntegerDivides F b w ∧
    (z : ℂ) = w / b ^ r

/-- Row contains an entry with reduced exponent r, PDF p.10. -/
def RowHasExponent (F : Subfield ℂ) (b : ℂ) (M : BlochMat)
    (i : Fin 3) (r : ℕ) : Prop := ∃ j, ReducedDenominator F b (M i j) r

/-- Row contains an entry whose normalized numerator is coprime to the base,
PDF pp.10,17. Zero entries are explicitly excluded. -/
def RowHasCoprime (F : Subfield ℂ) (b : ℂ) (M : BlochMat)
    (i : Fin 3) (r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ j : Fin 3, M i j ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ w : ℂ, IntegerCoprime F w b ∧
    (M i j : ℂ) = w / b ^ r

/-- All three clauses of Theorems 4.1 and 6.3, PDF pp.10,16-17.
Every comparison ranges over reduced nonzero entries. Row coprimality and
attainment of both maxima are retained, not just a row upper bound. -/
def DenominatorPattern (F : Subfield ℂ) (b : ℂ) (M : BlochMat)
    (N q : ℕ) (p : Fin 3) : Prop :=
  (∀ i j, M i j ≠ 0 → ∃ r, ReducedDenominator F b (M i j) r) ∧
  (∀ i j r, ReducedDenominator F b (M i j) r → r ≤ N) ∧
  (∃ i, RowHasExponent F b M i N) ∧
  ({i : Fin 3 | RowHasCoprime F b M i N} : Set (Fin 3)).ncard = 2 ∧
  (∃! i : Fin 3, ¬ RowHasExponent F b M i N) ∧
  (∀ i : Fin 3, ¬ RowHasExponent F b M i N →
    (∀ j r, ReducedDenominator F b (M i j) r → r ≤ N - q) ∧
    RowHasExponent F b M i (N - q) ∧ RowHasCoprime F b M i (N - q) ∧ i = p)

/-- N=sum q_ai, PDF p.10. -/
def canonicalTotalWeight (n k : ℕ) (d : CanonicalData) : ℕ :=
  (d.1.map fun pa => denominatorWeight n k pa.2).sum

/-- Positive t with 2^t=-1 modulo the odd part s; add 1 avoids natural
negative integers. For s=1 this is true, as required, PDF p.13. -/
def MinusOneIsTwoPower (s : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ t : ℕ, 0 < t ∧ Nat.ModEq s (2 ^ t + 1) 0

/-- Actual z-rotations inside a matrix group, PDF p.12. -/
def zRotationsIn (G : Set Mat) : Set Mat :=
  {U | U ∈ G ∧ ∃ theta : ℝ, U = cyclotomicZRotation theta}

/-- Equation (27), with endpoint represented by Fin(2n), PDF p.12. -/
def finiteZRotations (n : ℕ) : Set Mat :=
  {U | ∃ j : Fin (2 * n), U = cyclotomicZRotation (Real.pi * j.val / n)}

/-- Equation (30), actual roots of unity, PDF p.13. -/
def finitePhases (n : ℕ) : Set ℂ :=
  {z | ∃ j : Fin (2 * n), z = cyclotomicRoot (2 * n) ^ j.val}

/-- Elements of R_n of complex modulus one, PDF p.13. -/
def unitPhases (n : ℕ) : Set ℂ := {z | z ∈ cyclotomicSynthesisRing n ∧ ‖z‖ = 1}

/-- f_N, PDF pp.13-14. N is cast before division. All uses have N positive even. -/
def equalityFraction (N : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  (2 / (N : ℝ)) * (((Finset.range (N + 1)).filter fun n =>
    0 < n ∧ Even n ∧ (cyclotomicGroup n : Set Mat) = ringUnitaries n).card : ℝ)

/-- Exactly the five parameters of Section 7 Parts 2-3, PDF pp.19-23. -/
def SmallParameter (n : ℕ) : Prop := n ∈ ({2, 4, 6, 8, 12} : Finset ℕ)

/-- The unique prime above 2 on the five parameters, PDF p.19.
Intersection of all primes containing 2 specifies it without choosing a
prime or assuming the source's uniqueness result as an input. Outside those
parameters no theorem uses this helper. -/
def twoPrime (n : ℕ) : Ideal (integerRing n) :=
  sInf {p : Ideal (integerRing n) | p.IsPrime ∧ (2 : integerRing n) ∈ p}

/-- Exponent of the prime ideal in an integral principal ideal, Definition 7.2,
PDF p.19. emultiplicity uses ideal multiplication, not element divisibility. -/
def integralValuation (n : ℕ) (z : integerRing n) : ℕ∞ :=
  emultiplicity (twoPrime n) (Ideal.span ({z} : Set (integerRing n)))

/-- Extended embedding that preserves infinity, PDF p.19. -/
def extendedOrder (v : ℕ∞) : EReal :=
  if v = ⊤ then ⊤ else (v.toNat : EReal)

/-- Additive ideal-normalized valuation on R_n, Definition 7.2, PDF p.19.
A least dyadic denominator clears z, then its contribution to the valuation
is subtracted. Both integral valuations are finite for nonzero arguments
on the five parameters. Zero stays +infinity. The off-ring value is -infinity
and is never used by the source statements. -/
def primeValuation (n : ℕ) (z : ℂ) : EReal :=
  if z = 0 then ⊤
  else if h : ∃ d : ℕ, z * (2 : ℂ) ^ d ∈ integerRing n then
    extendedOrder (integralValuation n
      ⟨z * (2 : ℂ) ^ Nat.find h, Nat.find_spec h⟩) -
      (Nat.find h : EReal) * extendedOrder (integralValuation n 2)
  else ⊥

/-- mu(x,y)=-min(v_p(x),v_p(y)), Definition 7.3, PDF p.20.
Normalized pairs have finite complexity even when one coordinate is zero. -/
def columnComplexity (n : ℕ) (x y : ℂ) : EReal :=
  -min (primeValuation n x) (primeValuation n y)

/-- mu_n=v_p(1+i), PDF p.20. -/
def smallComplexity (n : ℕ) : EReal := primeValuation n (1 + Complex.I)

/-- Literal binary integral-basis representative of Z[zeta_(2n)] mod 2,
PDF pp.21-22. It is an actual complex number, not an abstract residue class. -/
def IsBinaryRepresentative (n : ℕ) (z : ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ a : Fin (Nat.totient (2 * n)) → Fin 2,
    z = ∑ i, ((a i).val : ℂ) * cyclotomicRoot (2 * n) ^ i.val

/-- Mod 2 of the whole squared-modulus sum is zero, Lemma 7.5, PDF p.22. -/
def NormSumEven (n : ℕ) (a b : ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ q : integerRing n,
    ((Complex.normSq a + Complex.normSq b : ℝ) : ℂ) = 2 * (q : ℂ)

/-- The constructed pair (c_k,d_k), with order H0*Uz essential, PDF p.22. -/
def reducedColumn (n : ℕ) (x y : ℂ) (k : ℤ) : Bool → ℂ :=
  (hZero * cyclotomicZRotation (Real.pi * (k : ℝ) / n)).mulVec (fun b => if b then y else x)

/-! Small sanity examples pin conventions and off-domain behavior. -/

example : hZero false false = (1 + Complex.I) / 2 := rfl

example : QAlgorithms.QubitChannels.sigma 0 = QAlgorithms.pauliX := by simp [QAlgorithms.QubitChannels.sigma]

example : cyclotomicZRotation 0 = 1 := by ext a b; cases a <;> cases b <;> simp [cyclotomicZRotation]

example : synthesisWordMatrix 4 [] = 1 := rfl

example : synthesisWordCost [.rotation, .rotation] = 2 := rfl

example (D : Mat) : canonicalProduct 2 ([], D) = 1 := rfl

example : canonicalCost 2 ([], (1 : Mat)) = 0 := rfl

example (n : ℕ) : (0 : ℂ) ∈ cyclotomicSynthesisRing n := (cyclotomicSynthesisRing n).zero_mem

example (n : ℕ) : primeValuation n 0 = ⊤ := by simp [primeValuation]

example : extendedOrder ⊤ = ⊤ := by simp [extendedOrder]

example : MinusOneIsTwoPower 1 := by
  exact ⟨1, by decide, by decide⟩

example (theta : ℝ) : cyclotomicZRotation theta false false = 1 := rfl

example (theta : ℝ) : cyclotomicZRotation theta false true = 0 := by simp [cyclotomicZRotation]

example : hZero ∈ cliffordGroup := Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp)

